{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Build the Cinescope cinema seat-booking Angular app in the Nx workspace (project `cinescope`, `apps/cinescope`), implementing tickets 01–07 in `spec/tickets/` in order against `spec/README.md`. Do not ask questions; choose the simplest option where the spec is silent. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Angular 22 standalone components, zoneless, signals, `resource()` for async loading, `toSignal` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop`, `@if`/`@for` control flow, `ng-template` with `NgTemplateOutlet`.\n   - Angular Router: query param `date` for the movie list, route params `id`, `canActivate` guards (functional `CanActivateFn`).\n   - HttpClient (`provideHttpClient()` in app.config.ts) with firstValueFrom, talking to json-server at `http://localhost:3000`.\n   - Angular Material 22: mat-stroked-button, mat-flat-button, mat-form-field with matInput, mat-datepicker with native date adapter, mat-checkbox, MatSnackBar (toast via openFromComponent, MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA), FormsModule ngModel for checkout inputs.\n   - sessionStorage persistence of the booking (key `cinescope.booking`).\n   - Vitest unit tests via `@angular/build:unit-test`; Nx build/lint/test targets; pnpm 11.1.0.\n   - Pure modules for seat layout, pricing and checkout validation.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models.ts` (created): Movie, Screening, Reservation interfaces per spec 2.1.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/dates.ts` (created, then extended): toIsoDate, parseIsoDate (returns null for invalid), startOfToday, addDays, weekdayName, showDate(isoDate, time) → `Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/api.service.ts` (created, extended): BASE_URL `http://localhost:3000`; methods movies(), movie(id), screeningsOn(date) (query param date), screening(id), createReservation(body: Omit<Reservation,'id'>) (POST /reservations).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list/movie-list.component.{ts,html,scss}` (created): day picker with 5 buttons (data-testid day-button, data-date, data-selected) from `days` array; datepicker input data-testid date-picker with min=today, dateChange → navigate `?date=`; `selectedIso` computed from query param (invalid/past → today); `data = resource({params: selectedIso, loader: Promise.all(movies, screeningsOn)})`; loading/error/empty/list states; `cards` computed groups screenings by movie sorted by time; openScreening navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/auditorium.ts` (created, extended): AUDITORIUM (15 rows; left block null for rows 1–10; middle 5–20; right 21–24; couches in row 15 via cellsBetween), SeatCell{kind:'seat',row,column,accessible}, CouchCell{kind:'couch',row,start,end}, Cell, seatId, cellIds, cellStartColumn, cellLabel, compareCells.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/auditorium.spec.ts` (created): 308 selectable, 296 seats, 12 couches, 6 accessible in row 1, left-block rule. Passing.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-map/seat-map.component.{ts,html,scss}` (created, extended): loads screening and movie via resource (on failure navigate to `/`); calls booking.begin(id) on load; `stateOf(cell, occupied)` → unavailable / selected / accessible / available; `onCellClick` toggles if not unavailable; `selectedRows` computed; `cancel()` clears booking and goes to `/`; `continue()` navigates to summary when seatCount > 0; template has title, subtitle `Show Date: …`, seat-limit-info, screen-indicator, seat-map with seat-row, row labels, aisle elements, legend (legend-item data-state), selected-seats panel, Cancel/Continue buttons (continue-button disabled when seatCount === 0). Colours: #2E7D32, #F9A825, #C62828, #1565C0 in scss via data-state.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/toast.service.ts` (created): ToastComponent (template `<div data-testid=\"toast\">{{ message }}</div>`), ToastService.show(message) using MatSnackBar.openFromComponent with duration 4000.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.service.ts` (created, rewritten several times): MAX_SEATS=10; Booking {screeningId, seats: Cell[], form: CheckoutValues, paidEmail?: string} stored in sessionStorage key `cinescope.booking`; readBooking() with try/catch; signals screeningId, seats, form, paidEmail, seatCount (couch=2), total (priceOf sum); begin(id) (new empty booking if different screening or paid); isSelected; toggle(cell) (removes if selected; toasts `Maximum 10 seats per booking` when over limit); updateForm; markPaid(email); clear(); private writeSeats and store (writes sessionStorage).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/pricing.ts` (created): priceOf (couch 89; rows 1–5 → 25; 6–10 → 32; else 39); formatPrice → `xx.xx PLN`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.guard.ts` (created): bookingInProgressGuard (screeningId matches route id, seatCount > 0, paidEmail null, else UrlTree `/`); bookingPaidGuard (paidEmail !== null else `/`).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/summary/summary.component.{ts,html,scss}` (created): loads screening and movie (redirect on failure); items computed (sorted with compareCells, key, row, seat description `12` or `Couch 3-4`, price); totalText `Total: <sum> PLN`; remove(cell) toggles and goes to seats when empty; back() → seats; confirm() → checkout. Data-testids per spec 9.3.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/checkout.ts` (created): CheckoutValues, CheckoutField, CheckoutErrors, CHECKOUT_FIELDS, EMPTY_CHECKOUT, validateCheckout (exact messages from spec 7; EMAIL regex `^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$`; PHONE `^\\d{9}$`; no trimming).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/checkout.spec.ts` (created): validation tests. Passing.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/checkout/checkout.component.{ts,html,scss}` (created): values = booking.form; errors computed; touched signal set; error(field) shown only when touched; update() writes booking form; touch() on blur/change; back() → summary; pay(): if errors → touch all, toast `The form contains errors`; else createReservation with sorted seat ids flatMapped, customer, totalPrice; on success booking.markPaid(email) and navigate `/confirmation`; on failure toast `Payment failed. Please try again.` and re-enable. Button text `Processing…` while submitting, otherwise `Pay <total> PLN`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/confirmation/confirmation.component.{ts,html,scss}` (created): heading `Payment successful`; message `Your tickets will be sent shortly to {{ booking.paidEmail() }}`; continue() clears booking and goes to `/`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts` (rewritten): `''` → MovieListComponent; `screenings/:id/seats` → SeatMapComponent; `screenings/:id/summary` → SummaryComponent with bookingInProgressGuard; `screenings/:id/checkout` → CheckoutComponent with bookingInProgressGuard; `confirmation` → ConfirmationComponent with bookingPaidGuard; `**` → redirect to `''`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts` (modified): added provideHttpClient() alongside provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners, provideRouter(appRoutes), provideNativeDateAdapter().\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/placeholder/` (created in ticket 01, then deleted in ticket 06).\n   - Workspace: `pnpm-lock.yaml` untouched by me. Untracked `/workspace/project/.pnpm-store/` created by my accidental pnpm install (not yet removed). `dist/` produced by builds (gitignored).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `pnpm nx build` failed with ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY (pnpm wanted to purge node_modules with no TTY). I then ran `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --offline --config.confirmModulesPurge=false`, which recreated node_modules and failed offline (ERR_PNPM_NO_OFFLINE_TARBALL for @angular/cdk). Fix: reran `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --config.confirmModulesPurge=false` with network, which succeeded. This was self-inflicted and should be disclosed to the user; the install resolved versions slightly newer than the lockfile's ranges may suggest (for example @angular/router 22.0.8, @angular/build 22.0.9), so the user should know that.\n   - Ticket 03 duplicate toast: the seat map component also called toast on the limit after BookingService already did; removed the component-side toast.\n   - Ticket 04 build: none. Summary import blank-line glitch was attempted to be fixed but the Edit failed; the blank line remains (harmless).\n   - Ticket 05 TS2783 \"'form' is specified more than once\" in readBooking; fixed by reading stored booking as plain `Booking`.\n   - Ticket 05: checkout.component.ts initially included an unnecessary screening-loading resource and an unused import; rewritten without them.\n   - Routes edit failed once because the file had changed; fixed by rewriting app.routes.ts fully.\n   - Smoke test: `curl` not installed (replaced with Node fetch). First json-server instance was already running; second start got EADDRINUSE on `::1:3000`. Node fetch to 127.0.0.1 gets ECONNREFUSED, but `[::1]:3000/movies` returns 200 and `[::1]:4200/screenings/1/seats` returns 200 with `<app-root`. No user feedback on these errors.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: builds for tickets 01–06 pass; `pnpm nx lint cinescope` passes; `pnpm nx test cinescope` passes (12 tests). Dev server and API respond over IPv6 localhost.\n   - Ongoing/unsolved: no browser or Playwright on the machine (python3 and curl also missing), so no UI or flow verification was done. The movie list will show \"No screenings on this day\" for the current date (2026-11-03) because db.json screenings are 15–21 Sep 2026; per spec this is expected. End-to-end flows can be checked by navigating directly to `/screenings/1/seats` (route works regardless of date). Production bundle warns over the 500 kB budget (about 609 kB; warning only).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial request (the only user message besides a later system-style notice about output token limits, which is not a user request): \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   - A later message said the output token limit was hit and asked to resume without apology or recap, breaking remaining work into smaller pieces. A message updated the working directory to `/workspace/project/apps/cinescope`, later back to `/workspace/project`.\n   - The current message asks for a text-only summary with no tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Run a final `pnpm nx build cinescope --skip-nx-cache` and confirm success (last build after ticket 06 changes succeeded; no changes since except a spec file and test runs).\n   - Remove the stray untracked `/workspace/project/.pnpm-store/` directory created by my accidental install (check it is not in use first), and stop the background `pnpm api` and `pnpm nx serve cinescope` processes (cannot use `ps`; use `pkill` or similar carefully).\n   - Tell the user about the node_modules recreation incident and the reinstall.\n   - Optionally tick the checkboxes in spec/tickets/*.md (ticket 07 requires all acceptance criteria met; not done).\n   - Tell the user that the UI was not verified in a browser (no browser available) and that the production bundle exceeds the 500 kB soft budget.\n   - Decide whether to commit; no commit has been requested, so do not commit without asking.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Ticket 07 (final pass) verification. Lint and unit tests pass. I started json-server and the dev server in the background. Node fetch to `127.0.0.1:3000` and `127.0.0.1:4200` gets ECONNREFUSED, but `[::1]:3000/movies` returns 200 with movie data and `[::1]:4200/screenings/1/seats` returns 200 with `app-root`. I was about to finish the smoke check with the IPv6 URLs, then do the final build.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run `pnpm nx build cinescope --skip-nx-cache` once more to confirm it succeeds, then clean up the stray `.pnpm-store/` directory and the background servers, and report to the user: all tickets' code is implemented, the build succeeds, lint and 12 unit tests pass, the node_modules incident and its reinstall, and that the UI was not exercised in a browser. This follows the user's instruction to finish only when every ticket is done and the build succeeds.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/7c6b26fa-c2b4-46c3-bcb4-060f368422ad.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c6b26fa-c2b4-46c3-bcb4-060f368422ad","uuid":"43ce452d-d0d8-443a-b15a-4b08ba8c38a9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:50:38.977Z","isSynthetic":true}
